# Generated build output — rendered manifests (dist/) and resolved
# lockfiles (*.lock). Worked examples are documentation: their inputs
# (aggregate, releases, manifests, catalogs, README) are committed; their
# generated output is not — it regenerates from those inputs. Ignored by
# default. If a specific artifact ever must ship, re-include it with an
# explicit negation — negate the directory AND its contents, since an
# excluded parent dir can never have a child re-included, e.g.:
#   !language-reference/examples/<name>/dist/
#   !language-reference/examples/<name>/dist/**
dist/
*.lock
# entity.lock is NOT a resolution lockfile: it is the per-entity pin
# record the pin step writes beside an entity for its author to commit.
# The glob above cannot tell the two apart, so it is re-included here.
!entity.lock
# Per-workspace resolution cache for worked examples. Pure build artifact
# (the artifact cache a pull fills); regenerates from the committed inputs via
# `aggrega pull`. In docs examples nothing authored lives under .aggrega/ — the
# lockfile ships beside the release as *.lock (ignored above), not here.
.aggrega/
search-refusals.log
# The translation package, installed by hand or by the translation workflows
# with `npm install --no-save` at the repository root.
/node_modules/
